    "body": "HTML 4.01 Specification might be a reference.\r\n\r\n\r\nhttps://www.w3.org/TR/1999/REC-html401-19991224/interact/forms.html#h-17.12.1\r\n17.12.1 Disabled controls - HTML 4.01 Specification\r\n> How disabled elements are rendered depends on the user agent. For example, some user agents \"gray out\" disabled menu items, button labels, etc.\r\n\r\n\r\nhttps://www.w3.org/TR/1999/REC-html401-19991224/interact/forms.html#h-17.12.2\r\n17.12.2 Read-only controls - HTML 4.01 Specification\r\n> How read-only elements are rendered depends on the user agent.\r\n\r\n\r\nIf there is large difference of rendering between user agents, it might have no choice but to specify as the above.\r\nBut I don't consider that there is large difference of rendering between major user agents.\r\nTherefore, I consider that it is also possible to specify in more detail.\r\n",
